{"school":{"dbn":"24Q125","name":"I.S. 125 Thom J. McCann Woodside","boro":"Queens","district":"24","district_label":"District 24","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":1150,"enrollment_year":"2025-26","address":"46-02 47 AVENUE, QUEENS, NY 11377","phone":"718-326-6210","website":"www.is125q.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/67699","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"IS 125Q is a vibrant learning community that reflects, not only the Woodside/Sunnyside neighborhoods, but the greater Queens borough. IS 125Q is a 2023 Respect for All Banner School. We use Restorative Practices to promote pro-social behaviors, address conflict through various Restorative Circles, peer-to-peer Conflict Resolution, as well as Tier 2 Restorative Interventions. We work closely with Ramapo for Children Organization in creating a fully restorative environment. Our students receive a supportive, inclusive, and differentiated education each school day. Our Arts Department offers students eight different learning paths: Band, Chorus, Dance, Digital Arts (3D Printing), Drama, Music Theory, Orchestra, and Visual Arts. Our students showcase their growth and mastery through multiple performances throughout the school year. Our aim is to have students perfect their artistic talents to prepare them for the competitive Performing Arts High Schools. We are also the home of the 2023 NYC Varsity Girls Middle School Basketball Champions. IS 125Q also offer boys\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0099 basketball and soccer in City and District League play. Our Regents program offers qualifying students the opportunity to enter high school with credit (when meeting Regents criteria) for four Regents exams: Algebra, 11th Grade English, 11th grade U.S. History and Government, and Earth Science, or Living Environment, as well as the foreign language proficiency exam in French or Spanish. IS 125Q offers students a variety of early morning and after school activities: Minecraft, Soccer, Volleyball, Badminton, Basketball, Spirit Squad, True Colors/GSA, Creative Writing, The Howler (School Paper), Student Government, The Green Team, Photography, Gardening, and Crafts. Our philosophy is that if our students want a club then we will find a teacher to lead it. Our offering will always reflect the interests of our students. Our students are also offered tutoring, Regents prep, and SHSAT prep throughout the school year. We partner with New York Edge, which serves 200 students each day for three hours after school. Our STEM program is linked with NY Sunworks and IS 125Q is moving to incorporate Project Based Learning in STEM with Generation Citizen to address local Woodside/Sunnyside issues. IS 125Q is a forward moving, problem-solving, collaborative community that creates strong connections with families to ensure the social and academic success of our students. Check out our Instagram page: @IS125Q. Let\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0099s go Wolves!","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":"7 to Bliss St-46th St","bus":"B24, Q104, Q32, Q39, Q60, Q67","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Sunnyside","latitude":40.7405,"longitude":-73.9188,"coordinate_source":"points","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2025-26"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.927],"n":[777.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.952,0.956,0.907,0.93,0.923,0.916,0.922],"n":[1564.0,1496.0,1407.0,1620.0,1595.0,1662.0,1436.0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null,1.0,0.908]},"attendance_remote_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.903],"n":[1403.0]},"chronic_absent_ems_all":{"y":["2015-16","2016-17","2017-18","2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.884,0.88,0.874,0.872,0.886,0.